Onesimus Director – Hinweise zu Code von Dritten / Third-party notices
======================================================================

Onesimus Director is a Rust re-implementation of Bareos. Some Bareos source
files are themselves taken from other projects and carry the notices of these
projects. Where this code was ported to Rust, the notices are kept here and in
the SPDX headers of the Rust files. Stand: 2026-11-23. Not legal advice.

The notices below are reproduced from the Bareos sources
(https://github.com/bareos/bareos, branch master, core/src/...).

Summary
-------

| Component                | Rust file                              | Licence           | Origin in Bareos                         |
|--------------------------|----------------------------------------|-------------------|------------------------------------------|
| FastLZ                   | crates/bareos-format/src/compression.rs | MIT               | core/src/fastlz/src/fastlz.c             |
| fastlzlib (block stream) | crates/bareos-format/src/compression.rs | MIT               | core/src/fastlz/src/fastlzlib.c          |
| LZ4                      | crates/bareos-format/src/compression.rs | BSD-2-Clause      | core/src/fastlz/src/lz4.c                |
| OpenBSD fnmatch()        | crates/ofd/src/fnmatch.rs               | BSD-3-Clause      | core/src/lib/fnmatch.cc (OpenBSD 1.6)    |
| OSSP var                 | crates/odir/src/expand.rs               | OSSP permissive (LicenseRef-OSSP-var) | core/src/lib/var.cc, var.h |

Only the decoders (FastLZ levels 1 and 2, LZ4 block decoder) and the
algorithms of fnmatch() and OSSP var were ported; no C code is shipped.

Checked and not ported (no notice required):
 - CRC-32 (crates/bareos-format/src/volume.rs): the standard polynomial
   0xEDB88320 with a table computed at compile time; Bareos' crc32.cc
   (S. Brumme) is not copied.
 - MD5, SHA, HMAC, Base64, TLS: from the Rust crates listed in Cargo.lock
   (md-5, sha2, hmac, base64, rustls, openssl); the Bareos Base64 variant is
   Bareos' own code (AGPL-3.0-only, see LICENSE).
 - liblzo2 is not part of the program; it is loaded at run time if installed
   (GPL-2.0-or-later, separate package).

Rust dependencies
-----------------

The binaries link the Rust crates of Cargo.lock (mostly MIT or Apache-2.0).
Their licence texts are available with `cargo about` / `cargo license`; the
policy is enforced in CI by `cargo deny` (deny.toml). The i386 package of osd
is built with `vendored-openssl` and contains OpenSSL (Apache-2.0;
https://www.openssl.org/source/license.html).


